      "id": 1,
      "text": "Tillery was incorporated as a town in 1889, marking its formal establishment in Halifax County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tillery%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1936 the community was renamed Roanoke Farms, reflecting a shift in its agricultural identity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tillery%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lake Tillery was formed by damming the Pee Dee River, a waterway born from the Yadkin and Uwharrie Rivers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.laketillery.com/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Tillery History House museum sits on former plantation land worked by generations of African‑American enslaved people.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visithalifax.com/listing/NqyG/the-tillery-history-house",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Tillery Chapel Rosenwald School, built under a federal program, served the community until its closure in 1981.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tillery%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
